 6. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Specter, which features a swappable nose. Photo: Courtesy of Aevex

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 💥 Aevex unveiled Specter, a turbojet-powered "one-way attack platform" developed alongside advanced manufacturer Divergent . The companies teased ground- and air-launched variants.

 Why it matters: "Specter reflects our lessons learned on capability from delivering thousands of autonomous systems in theater," Aevex's chief technology officer, Manan Patel, said in a statement. 💭 My thought bubble: At what point does a drone become a missile? A missile become a drone? 🧰 Traysar revealed it's developing Terminus, a truck-mounted boring machine. The subterranean startup is also partnering with Armada, known for its mobile data centers .

 Why it matters: The underground domain is heating up, fueled by Palmer Luckey's teases as well as tunnel-clearing clashes and bunker-busting bombing campaigns in the Middle East. 💭 My thought bubble: Traysar CEO Yadin Soffer made his case on "The Drone Ultimatum" podcast this summer. It's worth a listen. 
 
